From 0debeab375cb45e2af9c35ee116b5c7eb6d60391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lance-index-build <lance-index-build@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bench(index): stream the base from disk; MS MARCO v2.1
 dataset; targets

Scale runs (MS MARCO v2.1, 113.5M x 1024 float32, 465 GB) cannot hold the
base in memory. The runner now reads base vectors by row range for
ingestion, sampling and ground truth. New DATASET=msmarco reads the
base.fbin / query.fbin / gt.ibin written by prepare_msmarco.py, with the
published top-1000 as ground truth. With N_LIMIT, exact ground truth for
the first GT_QUERIES queries is computed by a streaming scan of the base
and cached next to the dataset. TARGET_* limits record pass/fail per
build (build time, index size, peak RSS, best recall at TARGET_K within
the latency limit). The assignment-quality sample is drawn with a sparse
Fisher-Yates that picks the same rows as before without materializing
every row id.
